{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"126","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Password"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Asterix, Obelix and their temporary buddies Suffix and Prefix has finally found the Harmony temple. However, its doors were firmly locked and even Obelix had no luck opening them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A little later they found a string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":", carved on a rock below the temple's gates. Asterix supposed that that's the password that opens the temple and read the string aloud. However, nothing happened. Then Asterix supposed that a password is some substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prefix supposed that the substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the beginning of the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":"; Suffix supposed that the substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" should be the end of the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":"; and Obelix supposed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" should be located somewhere inside the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":", that is, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" is neither its beginning, nor its end."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Asterix chose the substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" so as to please all his companions. Besides, from all acceptable variants Asterix chose the longest one (as Asterix loves long strings). When Asterix read the substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" aloud, the temple doors opened. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You know the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":". Find the substring "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" or determine that such substring does not exist and all that's been written above is just a nice legend."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" whose length can vary from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"106"},{"kind":"text","text":" (inclusive), consisting of small Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":". If a suitable "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" string does not exist, then print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Just a legend"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" without the quotes."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"childre